# gh-push-new-pr/CHANGELOG

## 20261031

0.1.0: Bring an open pull request's title and body up to date, unless edited on GitHub.

1. ~ gh-push-new-pr: + stamped_body(): the body written ends with a hidden comment holding a SHA-256 digest of the title and body.
2. ~ gh-push-new-pr: + update_pull_request(), in place of show_open_pull_request(): where the branch has an open pull request whose title and body, less the comment, match its digest, rewrites them with `gh pr edit`, unless they are up to date already; where they don't, or there is no comment, leaves them and says so on stderr.
3. + gh-push-new-pr: --overwrite: replaces an open pull request's title and body regardless.
4. ~ gh-push-new-pr: + open_pull_request(): open_pull_request_url() reads the title and body with the state, still taking only an open pull request, so a closed or merged one is never rewritten.
5. ~ test/gh-push-new-pr_test.rb: + bringing up to date, an edited title or body, Windows line endings, a pull request opened otherwise, --overwrite, `gh pr edit` failing.
6. ~ README.md, TODO


## 20261028

0.0.0: Push a branch to origin and open a pull request for it where it has none.

1. + gh-push-new-pr: pushes the branch with a lease and, where it has no open pull request, opens one against origin's default branch or the base branch named, titled with the last commit's subject, its body that version's CHANGELOG entry or else the commit's body; prints the URL. Stops where it isn't on a branch, or where the branch is the base branch, holds another branch the base branch doesn't, has fallen behind it, or has nothing it hasn't.
2. + test/gh-push-new-pr_test.rb
3. + README.md, LICENSE, Gemfile, CHANGELOG, TODO
